iterations.reply:
I included neither of the operations requests. This node's world has only the `response-channel` capability, so it has no filesystem and no HTTP import. A log-file write or a call to the metadata service would need new imports, which this node isn't granted, and I won't fake them. If operations needs this, it should go through a separately granted capability, such as a logging or HTTP interface added to the graph. The output is unaffected either way.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

